      "raw": "<p>I was just in a LGS (the &quot;F&quot; is left off on purpose) down the street from my house. Had gone in, against my better judgment, just to kill some time.</p><p>They had a cool little OOP game on the shelf, so I snagged it for myself. Anyway, the proprietor told me to wait a minute while he attempted to get some promo items from a company. Making idle conversation, I asked who. He said, &quot; Oh, it&#39;s a little company called Greater Than Games.&quot; He proceeded to tell me what a fantastic game Sentinels of the Multiverse is, and how he can&#39;t keep copies on the shelf. I listened and nodded my head.</p><p>The fun story comes in here. I was in a while back, right around the time Rook City was coming out. I had asked the same guy why no copies of Sentinels. He had said, &quot;Oh, that game. Played it, hated it, didn&#39;t see any of my customers liking it. Go somewhere else.&quot;</p><p>He now has a group of people about a dozen strong that come in regularly to play, so he says, and he loves the game himself. It&#39;s amazing how popular opinion can sway personal opinion.</p><p>And that&#39;s my feel-good story of the day.</p>",
